---

Put the @vermicelli rice noodles{250%g} into a bowl and cover with boiling water. Leave them to soak for ~{4%minutes} and then drain them.

Soak the @dried shrimp{50%g}(or 100 g small frozen prawns) in the @Chinese cooking wine (or sherry){125%ml}, then heat the @garlic oil{1%tbsp} in a #wok and fry the @Chinese leaf{100%g}(finely sliced), @baby corn{125%g}(sliced into thin rounds), and @spring onions{2}(finely sliced) for a ~{2%minutes}.

Add the @Madras curry powder, medium{2%tsp} and @fresh ginger{1%tsp}(finely chopped) to the wok, and then the @chicken stock{250%ml} and @soy sauce{3%tbsp}. Pour in the shrimps, with their wine, and the drained, soaked noodles, tossing and shaking everything all together in the wok.

Finally, stir in the @bean sprouts{150%g} and give a final toss, before turning out into a bowl and sprinkling with the @fresh coriander{4%tbsp}(chopped). Serve with @./Savoury/Seared Salmon{}.